# A template of a script, run stepped as `save-quit-script` is, with the
# same setup: `@FILE@` stands for `/fixture/note.txt`, a copy of `note.txt`
# in the file fake's model. The run must leave the copy holding the bytes
# of `note-expected`, and print no `commands:` line. The quit waits for the
# save, so the script has a `join` after the `wq` line, which ends when the
# save's result has ended the loop.

# `e` opens the file, and `join` waits for the load's result.
run ex
commit e @FILE@
key <Enter> Enter -
join

# The buffer is modified.
key i KeyI -
commit zero
key <Escape> Escape -

# `wq` starts the save and asks the editor to quit. The quit waits for the
# save, so the loop is still running after the accept key: `join` waits for
# the save's result, whose delivery ends the loop. Without the wait the
# `show` line would be handled while the save runs and print a `commands:`
# line, and the end of the script would stop the loop, which cancels the
# save.
run ex
commit wq
key <Enter> Enter -
join
show
